# Line endings.
#
# Every text file is stored LF in the object database and checked out LF on
# every platform. Without the `eol=lf` half, a Windows checkout gets CRLF while
# .prettierrc pins `endOfLine: "lf"` — so `npm run format:check` fails on files
# nobody touched, and the only way to "fix" it is a repo-wide rewrite that
# buries the real change. CI (Linux) never saw the problem, which is the worst
# shape a divergence can take: green there, red here.
#
# Applying this to an existing clone needs one renormalisation pass on a CLEAN
# tree — `git add --renormalize .` then commit — otherwise the change only
# lands file by file as they are next touched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Lockfiles are generated: keep them out of diffs by default.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
